TrueSignal
==========

TrueSignal is a modified version of HoneyWire
(https://github.com/andreicscs/HoneyWire), originally written by
Andrea Termine and released under the GNU Affero General Public License
version 3 (see LICENSE). All upstream copyright notices are retained.

Modifications (AGPLv3 section 5(a))
-----------------------------------
2026-10-19  Imported from HoneyWire v2.1.0.
2026-10-19  Rebranded to TrueSignal: product name, UI, logo, documentation,
            Go module paths, CLI binary (`truesignal`), host paths
            (/opt/truesignal, /etc/truesignal), container and image names,
            syslog app-name and SD-ID, environment variable prefix
            (HW_ -> TS_), sensor ID prefix (hw-sensor- -> ts-sensor-),
            node key prefix (hw_key_ -> ts_key_), session cookie
            (hw_auth -> ts_auth), and distribution endpoints (images,
            sensor registry, installer, release checks).

2026-10-23  Added the Identity Decoy sensor (Sensors/official/IdentityDecoy),
            a Go reimplementation of the LDAP, LDAPS and RDP honeypot
            concepts from Trapster Community
            (https://github.com/0xBallpoint/trapster-community) by
            0xBallpoint, GNU Affero General Public License v3 or later.
            The protocol behaviour is re-derived; no Trapster source is
            copied. The Go code, the TrueSignal SDK integration and the
            credential-capture policy are TrueSignal's.

Source for any network-accessible deployment of TrueSignal must be made
available to its users as required by AGPLv3 section 13.
